{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"e91b17d9-1aed-4c06-b91f-320244b5bd6e","step":{"id":"s1","script":"A standing wave has fixed nodes that never move. Here, both ends and the midpoint are nodes.","ops":[{"op":"text","id":"title","region":"A1","content":"Standing waves on a string"},{"op":"figure","id":"string","region":"right","frame":{"x":[-0.4,4.4],"y":[-1.5,1.5],"axes":"none"},"marks":[{"kind":"segment","from":[0,0],"to":[4,0],"stroke":"dashed"},{"kind":"fn","id":"crest","y":"sin(pi*x/2)","domain":[0,4]},{"kind":"point","id":"node0","at":[0,0],"label":"N"},{"kind":"point","id":"node2","at":{"on":"crest","x":2},"label":"N"},{"kind":"point","id":"node4","at":[4,0],"label":"N"}]},{"op":"text","id":"nodes","anchor":{"el":"title","side":"below","gap":0.08},"content":"Nodes: zero displacement"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"e91b17d9-1aed-4c06-b91f-320244b5bd6e","step":{"id":"s2","script":"Antinodes move the most. The dashed curve shows the string half a cycle later; nodes stay still while each loop reverses.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"oscillate","on":"string","marks":[{"kind":"fn","y":"-sin(pi*x/2)","domain":[0,4],"stroke":"dashed"},{"kind":"point","id":"anti1","at":{"on":"crest","x":1},"label":"A"},{"kind":"point","id":"anti3","at":{"on":"crest","x":3},"label":"A"},{"kind":"segment","from":[1,-0.8],"to":[1,0.8],"arrow":true},{"kind":"segment","from":[3,0.8],"to":[3,-0.8],"arrow":true}]},{"op":"text","id":"antinodes","anchor":{"el":"nodes","side":"below","gap":0.08},"content":"Antinodes: maximum motion"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"e91b17d9-1aed-4c06-b91f-320244b5bd6e","step":{"id":"s3","script":"Neighboring nodes are half a wavelength apart. An antinode lies halfway between them, a quarter wavelength from either node.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"spacing","on":"string","marks":[{"kind":"measure","from":[0,-1.25],"to":[2,-1.25],"label":"λ/2"},{"kind":"measure","from":[0,1.3],"to":[1,1.3],"label":"λ/4"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"distances","anchor":{"el":"antinodes","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"d_{NN}=\\frac{\\lambda}{2},\\qquad d_{NA}=\\frac{\\lambda}{4}"}],"checkpoint":{"question":"What distinguishes a node from an antinode?","expected_gist":"A node never moves; an antinode has maximum oscillation amplitude."}}}
